# Design System

## Brand direction

Use a trustworthy, calm, modern healthcare identity. The supplied Sharma
Clinic reference PDF is a visual starting point: - Page 1: blue
navigation bar, large healthcare hero, supporting feature cards. - Page
2: doctor cards, specialty filters, services, and split content
section. - Page 3: health article/blog cards and a structured footer.

Use these as inspiration, not as a pixel-perfect copy. The reference
includes placeholder/non-clinic content; do not reproduce unrelated
ecommerce copy, product shopping UI, or invented claims.

## Visual language

-   Primary: professional clinic blue.
-   Supporting: white, light neutral backgrounds, subtle teal accents.
-   Use restrained shadows, clear borders, generous whitespace, and
    readable contrast.
-   Typography should be clean and accessible; establish consistent
    heading, body, label, and caption scales.
-   Use Lucide React icons consistently. Avoid emoji as interface icons.
-   Use real clinic/doctor imagery only when supplied or approved. Do
    not invent doctor identities, credentials, or testimonials.

## Responsive behavior

Design mobile-first. Public pages, booking forms, tables, calendars, and
dashboards must work on small screens. Tables may become stacked cards
on mobile where appropriate.

## Components

Prefer shadcn/ui primitives and shared wrappers. Build consistent: -
Header/navigation and footer - Buttons, form fields, validation
messages - Doctor cards and service cards - Appointment status badges -
Data tables, filters, pagination - Dashboard summary cards and charts -
Confirmation dialogs and toast feedback

## Accessibility

Use semantic HTML, keyboard-operable controls, visible focus states,
associated labels, accessible dialogs, sufficient contrast, and
meaningful image alt text.

## UX rules

-   Show loading, empty, success, and error states.
-   Confirm destructive actions.
-   Do not communicate payment success until server-side verification
    confirms it.
-   Clearly display appointment date, time, doctor, fee, and payment
    state before checkout.
-   Avoid exposing patient details in public pages or URLs.
